WEBVTT

01:41.000 --> 01:43.770
MOTLEY HEROES

01:41.480 --> 01:44.110
I used the thermography from
the artificial satellite Shoji Peeper

01:44.110 --> 01:47.400
to check the number of monsters
inside the enemy's hideout.

01:47.440 --> 01:50.160
Thermal readings show that
there appear to be 500 monsters.

01:50.360 --> 01:51.490
If you do the simple math

01:51.490 --> 01:53.870
that means each of us has to
take down over 60 monsters.

01:54.160 --> 01:57.200
The only concern would be the strength
of the enemy's top-level monsters.

01:57.370 --> 01:59.580
We now know that Centichoro,
who appeared the other day

01:59.580 --> 02:02.460
was also working for
the Monster Association

02:02.670 --> 02:05.300
so we should assume that they have
several other monsters

02:05.300 --> 02:07.630
at threat-level Demon or even Dragon.

02:07.880 --> 02:12.800
I was guarding the headquarters,
so I only fought one parasite.

02:12.930 --> 02:15.220
What about you guys
who were fighting out there?

02:15.390 --> 02:16.680
Were they strong?

02:16.810 --> 02:19.020
It felt like a real mixed bag.

02:19.390 --> 02:22.650
Most of them weren't much,
but there were a few really nasty ones

02:22.810 --> 02:25.110
and even I had some close calls.

02:25.270 --> 02:26.860
CRACKING

02:25.440 --> 02:30.200
Now that I've learned to accept the pain,
it's not gonna be a problem.

02:30.400 --> 02:33.200
Is it true that Drive Knight
got taken out?

02:33.450 --> 02:34.450
I don't know...

02:34.820 --> 02:37.160
He tortured a monster
and was the first to discover

02:37.160 --> 02:41.410
that their hideout was in City Z,
so he went to investigate.

02:41.620 --> 02:43.880
But we haven't heard from him since.

02:44.080 --> 02:46.340
So he was taken out, huh?

02:46.630 --> 02:49.380
He's got a cyborg body

02:49.380 --> 02:51.590
so it doesn't necessarily
mean that he's dead.

02:51.970 --> 02:55.180
Maybe his parts were destroyed,
and he can't move or send a signal

02:55.180 --> 02:57.720
so he's lying low somewhere
just waiting to be rescued.

02:58.350 --> 02:59.930
Let's hope so...

03:00.930 --> 03:05.360
What this means is, any of us
could end up like Drive Knight.

03:05.730 --> 03:07.320
So don't let your guard down.

03:07.400 --> 03:08.610
Stay sharp.

03:08.820 --> 03:11.570
I doubt they can defeat me.

03:11.650 --> 03:15.070
They'll strike without mercy
the minute we run into them.

03:15.320 --> 03:19.330
Of course, even if a monster
tries to negotiate

03:19.330 --> 03:20.950
we do not need to respond.

03:21.080 --> 03:24.420
That's right.
Showing mercy will get you killed.

03:24.500 --> 03:27.040
Can I say something?
Among the Monster Association

03:27.040 --> 03:30.880
there are also young men who
were tricked and turned into monsters.

03:31.340 --> 03:33.260
I want to save those guys.

03:33.590 --> 03:37.350
If you see monsters in prison uniforms,
let me deal with them.

03:37.680 --> 03:40.430
An old friend of mine turned
into a monster too

03:40.430 --> 03:42.180
so I had no choice but to slash him.

03:42.730 --> 03:45.650
Is there any way to save those
who've been monsterized?

03:45.980 --> 03:49.150
I plan on trying a combo of Angel Hug
and Awakening Deep Kiss

03:49.150 --> 03:51.820
to see if they can snap out of it.

03:51.940 --> 03:54.240
I see... Okay then... Sorry I asked.

03:54.360 --> 03:55.860
Let's get back to the topic.

03:56.030 --> 03:59.620
The boss, Monster King Orochi,
and the strategist, Gyoro-Gyoro

03:59.620 --> 04:01.790
are without a doubt
threat level-Dragon.

04:01.870 --> 04:06.540
Yeah, they're strong enough
to command this many monsters.

04:06.710 --> 04:09.670
We should avoid one-on-one fights
where possible.

04:09.750 --> 04:12.710
Fine, I'll take down the final boss.

04:12.920 --> 04:17.680
You guys handle the small fry
that get in my way, okay?

04:17.890 --> 04:19.470
Hey, don't make decisions
for everyone.

04:19.550 --> 04:21.760
So you're saying
you wanna fight the final boss?

04:21.760 --> 04:23.350
- Shut her up.
- I'm doing this for

04:23.350 --> 04:24.640
- This is pointless.
- you wimps.

04:24.640 --> 04:26.140
Now, now, you two...

04:26.770 --> 04:29.110
This is why I hate
managing Class-S heroes.

04:29.360 --> 04:32.780
We're not here to direct traffic.

04:33.230 --> 04:35.950
This is a hostage rescue mission.

04:36.070 --> 04:37.780
Monster hunting is only a bonus.

04:38.320 --> 04:41.120
Don't forget about that, Tornado.

04:41.200 --> 04:44.700
You'd better not launch an attack
that'll wipe out the entire hideout.

04:45.830 --> 04:48.040
The underground is quite vast and deep.

04:48.290 --> 04:49.540
Even with my investigation

04:49.540 --> 04:53.420
I can't pinpoint the exact location
of the boss in the hideout.

04:53.800 --> 04:56.720
If you run into something,
whether it be a small fry or the boss

04:56.720 --> 04:58.050
a fight is unavoidable.

04:58.340 --> 05:00.930
Anyone who encounters them
must take them out.

05:01.010 --> 05:04.100
If we'd known the boss's location or
where the hostages were ahead of time

05:04.100 --> 05:05.890
we could've done this
with far fewer people.

05:06.140 --> 05:09.940
Why do you think we've been
waiting around for everyone to gather?

05:10.440 --> 05:13.780
That much should be obvious
if you'd just think a little...

05:14.360 --> 05:16.360
Instead of always relying
on your psychic powers

05:16.400 --> 05:18.400
how about using your head
once in a while?

05:18.570 --> 05:21.280
Stop, stop! That's enough!

05:21.910 --> 05:22.740
Hey.

05:23.080 --> 05:26.290
You guys... I was wondering
why you weren't in the waiting room.

05:26.410 --> 05:29.580
I'm on the team, yet here you are,
having a secret meeting without me.

05:29.580 --> 05:30.710
What's the meaning of this?

05:30.750 --> 05:32.210
Amai Mask!

05:33.130 --> 05:36.210
We weren't trying
to exclude you or anything.

05:36.340 --> 05:38.420
We first wanted to discuss it
among Class-S heroes.

05:38.550 --> 05:40.090
Why only Class-S?

05:40.590 --> 05:43.140
There are other members on
the team like me, right?

05:43.140 --> 05:44.430
Um, well...

05:44.810 --> 05:48.060
<i>Everyone below Class-S is going</i>
<i>to be assigned to surface backup.</i>

05:48.310 --> 05:50.730
<i>I knew he would complain</i>

05:50.730 --> 05:53.440
<i>so I was going to tell him</i>
<i>at the last minute.</i>

05:54.020 --> 05:58.440
<i>How can I explain this</i>
<i>without hurting his pride?</i>

05:58.820 --> 06:01.280
Why? Because we all hate you.

06:01.320 --> 06:02.410
No, that's not true.

06:02.450 --> 06:05.080
You're making it worse, Tornado!

06:05.540 --> 06:08.750
Me assigned to surface standby?
Care to explain yourself?

06:08.910 --> 06:12.750
Yes, the attack team
goes underground

06:12.750 --> 06:15.460
and the support team stays above ground.
We split up into two teams.

06:15.590 --> 06:18.760
We wanted to utilize
your leadership skills and

06:18.760 --> 06:21.930
have you take command
of the support team, Amai Mask.

06:22.050 --> 06:24.850
We'll be the only ones
attacking underground.

06:25.100 --> 06:27.470
Deal with any monsters
we miss behind us.

06:27.850 --> 06:30.600
But I'll be bringing my disciples along.

06:30.690 --> 06:32.560
Twenty more pizzas, please.

06:32.730 --> 06:35.110
Don't stuff yourself before battle.

06:35.190 --> 06:37.190
Get protein instead, Pig God.

06:37.610 --> 06:40.280
No. I can't trust you guys
to handle it by yourselves.

06:40.400 --> 06:41.700
I'm going in too.

06:41.820 --> 06:43.320
<i>I knew he'd say that.</i>

06:43.490 --> 06:45.620
Do I have to spell it out for you?

06:45.740 --> 06:49.120
This fight is way out of your league.

06:49.200 --> 06:50.460
You're out of the lineup!

06:50.500 --> 06:52.540
Child Emperor,
you don't seem to understand.

06:52.540 --> 06:55.340
- Hey! Don't ignore me!
- If you want to utilize my leadership,

06:55.340 --> 06:58.050
then the Class-S heroes
should be under my command.

06:58.500 --> 07:00.720
- Us, under your command?
- Pretending not to hear me?!

07:00.720 --> 07:02.550
You're name is funny enough.

07:03.050 --> 07:06.220
You just want the credit?
Fine, take mine.

07:06.300 --> 07:08.100
But follow Child Emperor's orders.

07:08.260 --> 07:10.350
This isn't the time to be holding
each other back.

07:10.480 --> 07:11.480
That's right!

07:11.480 --> 07:14.440
You shouldn’t be putting on perfume
before a battle, you idiot!

07:14.650 --> 07:17.270
We're about to face
an army of monsters.

07:17.820 --> 07:19.860
This isn't the time to be
dragging each other down.

07:20.070 --> 07:23.070
- Zombieman, why are you immortal?
- You smell! Change your name!

07:23.110 --> 07:24.110
- It's creepy.

07:24.450 --> 07:27.080
Maybe you're actually a monster.

07:27.370 --> 07:28.410
What'd you just say?

07:28.530 --> 07:33.210
You're ranked Class S based
solely on your combat ability

07:33.250 --> 07:35.500
but your true identity is questionable.

07:35.710 --> 07:39.000
Can we really trust that
you're on our side?

07:39.210 --> 07:42.220
Hey now, stop pushing him.

07:42.340 --> 07:44.630
This isn't right.
Heroes shouldn't be fighting each other.

07:45.010 --> 07:47.550
Yeah, you're supposed to be a
pro hero, and yet...

07:47.680 --> 07:48.720
What the heck?

07:48.720 --> 07:53.560
If you've gotta problem,
forget the battle and go sing alone.

07:53.600 --> 07:56.770
You Class-S heroes acting
like you're above it all.

07:56.770 --> 07:58.310
Your arrogance has gone too far.

07:58.400 --> 08:00.690
You have a bad rep
in the Association.

08:01.190 --> 08:04.030
It doesn't look like
you're giving your best.

08:04.070 --> 08:07.160
Oh, and five more liters of cola, please.

08:07.320 --> 08:10.740
Aren't you forgetting the responsibility
that comes with power?

08:10.950 --> 08:11.870
Wait a sec!

08:11.870 --> 08:14.330
Why are you working as
an idol on the side?

08:14.330 --> 08:15.420
That's ridiculous.

08:15.420 --> 08:18.330
You call yourself Handsome Kamen,
but you're not even that good-looking!

08:18.380 --> 08:19.670
Do you get that?

08:19.790 --> 08:21.340
C-Calm down.

08:21.460 --> 08:24.130
If you piss off Amai Mask,
the media will tear you apart.

08:24.130 --> 08:24.970
It'll be trouble.

08:25.300 --> 08:30.010
You Class-S heroes only get to exist
because you're kept under control.

08:30.140 --> 08:34.140
Otherwise, you're just dangerous 
individuals with high combat power.

08:34.350 --> 08:36.980
So this time, I'll put you to good use.

08:37.100 --> 08:38.650
Follow my orders.

08:40.690 --> 08:44.150
<i>A master-servant relationship with</i>
<i>an assertive handsome guy.</i>

08:44.490 --> 08:46.450
<i>Not bad, but troubling...</i>

08:46.530 --> 08:49.240
Why not try and
make us obey by force?

08:49.450 --> 08:50.740
If you think you can.

08:51.830 --> 08:53.910
Do you think I can't?

08:56.500 --> 08:58.580
Hey, this is no joke.

08:58.580 --> 09:00.380
Stop that murderous glare, Flash.

09:00.460 --> 09:01.880
It's up to him.

09:01.960 --> 09:03.800
If he interferes with the operation...

09:03.840 --> 09:05.510
Mr. King has arrived!

09:06.630 --> 09:11.050
RUMBLE RUMBLE

09:11.260 --> 09:13.350
King, what perfect timing.

09:13.720 --> 09:15.350
You'll be under my command too...!?

09:15.680 --> 09:18.640
Why are you so filthy?
And you stink too.

09:18.850 --> 09:22.940
Oh yeah, I was brought here
right after I got home

09:23.070 --> 09:24.690
so I didn't have a chance to change.

09:25.110 --> 09:27.740
Oh dang,
this is gonna leave a stain.

09:27.820 --> 09:30.700
Why were you so late?
Where have you been?

09:30.870 --> 09:32.490
How did you get like that?

09:32.620 --> 09:33.950
<i>What's with the interrogation?</i>

09:34.160 --> 09:36.450
<i>I never did like this guy.</i>

09:36.700 --> 09:40.790
Well, it's not really anything
worth mentioning.

09:41.420 --> 09:43.000
But I was in City Z...

09:43.340 --> 09:44.750
- having hot pot...
- Mr. King was

09:44.750 --> 09:48.840
fighting alone near the enemy hideout
in City Z all night!

09:48.840 --> 09:49.680
Huh?

09:49.800 --> 09:51.840
The stains on his clothes
are the monsters' blood.

09:52.090 --> 09:55.010
As proof, the splatters
are only on the front.

09:55.140 --> 09:59.100
Outnumbered, he drained his strength
and pulled back.

09:59.100 --> 10:01.600
That's when we found him
and escorted him here!

10:01.600 --> 10:05.610
<i>Why do these people always get</i>
<i>the wrong idea and spread it around?</i>

10:05.780 --> 10:08.820
Fighting nonstop...all by himself...

10:10.490 --> 10:11.700
Impressive.

10:11.990 --> 10:16.740
Hmph... Your decisiveness,
your fearless resolve.

10:17.080 --> 10:18.750
I have to hand it to you.

10:18.910 --> 10:21.170
Apparently, there are
some decent Class-S heroes.

10:21.460 --> 10:23.170
Quarreling among ourselves
is pointless.

10:23.580 --> 10:25.750
For King's sake, I'll back down.

10:28.210 --> 10:29.720
But I'm still on the attack team.

10:29.800 --> 10:30.880
That's non-negotiable.

10:30.970 --> 10:33.340
<i>Incredible.</i>
<i>He's not backing down at all.</i>

10:34.140 --> 10:39.730
- King, you can't fight the enemy alone.
- No...

10:39.730 --> 10:44.190
Just like you, Drive Knight went alone
to investigate the ghost town

10:44.190 --> 10:46.070
and since then,
we've lost all contact with him.

10:46.860 --> 10:49.900
Who knows what kind of threat
might be lurking there?

10:50.070 --> 10:51.450
Let's all fight together.

10:53.860 --> 10:54.700
Sure...!

11:02.460 --> 11:04.210
The support team has assembled.

11:04.710 --> 11:05.960
It's time to depart.

11:08.590 --> 11:10.090
This is a critical moment.

11:10.420 --> 11:11.260
Yeah.

11:11.800 --> 11:13.680
Are you planning to go to the scene?

11:14.010 --> 11:16.390
As the one responsible,
I'll see this through to the end.

11:16.680 --> 11:20.180
I've underestimated you.
Who knew you had such backbone.

11:20.600 --> 11:23.480
I thought you were just driven
by ambition for promotion.

11:23.690 --> 11:25.810
Hmph. You're not wrong there.

11:25.980 --> 11:29.280
Defeating the Monster Association
will guarantee a promotion...

11:32.190 --> 11:34.320
And my name will go down in history.

11:40.750 --> 11:43.620
Thank you all for coming.
I'm Sekingal.

11:44.330 --> 11:45.460
And I'm Sitch.

11:45.580 --> 11:48.710
Is everyone clear on today's mission?

11:48.920 --> 11:53.340
Yes, sir! Today's event is
to support Class-S heroes.

11:53.470 --> 11:54.970
Um...okay...

11:55.180 --> 11:56.470
<i>Event?</i>

11:57.680 --> 12:01.310
Specifically, you will eliminate
any monsters who escape

12:01.310 --> 12:04.020
secure evacuation routes,
and protect the child.

12:04.270 --> 12:07.480
Once the Class-S heroes storm in
and rescue the hostage

12:07.480 --> 12:09.730
you will safely escort him
back to headquarters.

12:09.900 --> 12:12.070
That is the most important mission.

12:12.280 --> 12:13.570
Can I say something?

12:13.780 --> 12:14.610
What is it?

12:14.740 --> 12:17.990
We're risking our necks diving
straight into enemy territory

12:17.990 --> 12:20.030
without knowing what's waiting for us.

12:20.410 --> 12:25.210
At the very least,
I want my hero ranking bumped up.

12:25.330 --> 12:26.870
Otherwise, it ain't worth it.

12:28.420 --> 12:30.130
Fine. I promise.

12:30.250 --> 12:31.750
All right!

12:32.590 --> 12:33.670
Well, Sitch?

12:33.880 --> 12:37.340
Looks like humanity’s protectors
are stronger than ever, right?

12:37.550 --> 12:38.970
Uh...yeah...

12:39.180 --> 12:40.600
Excuse me, Mr. Sitch...

12:43.180 --> 12:44.020
What?!

12:48.440 --> 12:52.570
Yo, Sitch. I dropped
my portable phone somewhere.

12:52.820 --> 12:55.150
Sorry, but can you give me a new one?

12:55.490 --> 12:59.030
O-Okay. Got it.
I'll get you one right away.

12:59.530 --> 13:01.530
Remember, Sitch.

13:01.660 --> 13:03.580
Send him back
without telling him anything.

13:04.160 --> 13:07.290
And about Garou's hideout...

13:07.420 --> 13:09.500
Have you gotten any new information?

13:09.670 --> 13:13.130
I imagine he's still with
the monster group.

13:13.340 --> 13:16.130
No, nothing new.

13:16.670 --> 13:17.840
I see.

13:18.260 --> 13:19.300
Silverfang.

13:19.300 --> 13:20.140
Hm?

13:20.260 --> 13:22.850
Why did you let Garou get away?

13:23.430 --> 13:26.020
Did a monster really intervene?

13:26.430 --> 13:29.770
Are you saying
I let him go on purpose?

13:31.150 --> 13:34.940
Sorry... There's so much going on,
I'm a bit confused.

13:35.280 --> 13:38.570
I'll have a staff member
bring you a new transmitter.

13:38.780 --> 13:40.490
Please wait here.

13:43.160 --> 13:44.830
They don't trust you.

13:45.200 --> 13:49.120
Maybe they think you held back
and failed to finish him off.

13:49.330 --> 13:51.380
I didn't hold back.

13:52.670 --> 13:54.920
Good. Looks like no one's following me.

13:55.170 --> 13:57.670
For now, I'll hide in this room.

13:57.880 --> 13:59.930
But how am I gonna get out of here?

14:00.050 --> 14:01.430
What're you doing?

14:02.220 --> 14:03.850
Why are you here, Bang?

14:03.970 --> 14:07.890
I had some business to tend to.
Why are you here?

14:08.310 --> 14:10.900
There was an emergency summons
for Class-S heroes

14:10.900 --> 14:12.860
and I was brought here too...

14:13.270 --> 14:15.940
What? No one told me.

14:16.320 --> 14:19.490
Oops... I wasn't supposed to
tell Bang about this...

14:19.860 --> 14:23.740
Oh come on...
You and I shared a hot pot together.

14:23.870 --> 14:25.160
Spill it.

14:26.910 --> 14:29.710
King's taking a long time
in the bathroom.

14:30.210 --> 14:32.170
His engine was revving pretty hard

14:32.170 --> 14:34.590
so maybe he's just trying
to focus on his own.

14:36.250 --> 14:39.340
You're storming
the Monster Association's hideout?

14:39.510 --> 14:41.510
So that's what's happening...

14:42.340 --> 14:47.180
And yet, both Genos and I were left out.
I guess they don't trust us.

14:47.970 --> 14:51.730
They took a child hostage?
Damn brutes.

14:52.190 --> 14:56.190
We were so focused on tracking Garou,
we didn't even catch the news.

14:56.650 --> 15:00.990
Does Saitama know that
the enemy hideout is in the ghost town?

15:01.240 --> 15:02.820
No, I don't think so...

15:02.820 --> 15:05.070
If he knew, I'm sure he would've
already gone by himself.

15:05.530 --> 15:09.500
From here, the team will move
into the ruins of City Z

15:09.500 --> 15:11.870
each entering from their own route.

15:12.540 --> 15:14.210
But there's something
I want to ask you.

15:14.540 --> 15:16.380
Silverfang, Bomb.

15:16.840 --> 15:19.340
How about we take Caped Baldy
and Demon Cyborg along

15:19.460 --> 15:22.550
and secretly slip in
through my entry route?

15:23.010 --> 15:25.680
It would go against
the Association's orders though...

15:26.180 --> 15:28.140
Garou will be there, right?

15:28.560 --> 15:30.060
We'll go with you.

15:31.640 --> 15:32.690
All right.

15:32.940 --> 15:35.810
Just like yesterday,
we'll meet up at Saitama's place.

15:35.940 --> 15:37.230
Okay.

15:37.690 --> 15:39.280
See you later.

15:40.820 --> 15:44.490
<i>Oh, thank god. What a relief.</i>

15:45.490 --> 15:49.290
Oh, King's back.
Did something happen?

15:49.450 --> 15:51.500
No, no problem at all.

15:51.620 --> 15:54.080
<i>The King Engine has stopped.</i>

15:54.250 --> 15:56.040
<i>He must've sharpened his focus.</i>

15:57.130 --> 15:58.210
All right, let's head out.

15:58.670 --> 16:00.210
Is everyone ready?

16:00.960 --> 16:01.840
Let's go!!

16:11.930 --> 16:14.690
<i>I was summoned to</i>
<i>join the assault team</i>

16:14.770 --> 16:17.100
<i>but for some reason,</i>
<i>they pulled me out at the last minute.</i>

16:17.520 --> 16:19.610
<i>I was told to stay out of this matter.</i>

16:20.230 --> 16:23.030
<i>I bet Tornado's the one</i>
<i>who shut me out.</i>

16:23.150 --> 16:24.030
No!

16:24.360 --> 16:26.780
<i>She will never acknowledge me,</i>
<i>will she?</i>

16:27.200 --> 16:29.950
<i>I also have a personal score</i>
<i>to settle with the Monster Association.</i>

16:30.200 --> 16:34.000
<i>How dare they humiliate me</i>
<i>in front of my sister like that.</i>

16:35.290 --> 16:38.830
<i>Steady point-gathering</i>
<i>and continuous activity</i>

16:38.830 --> 16:40.750
<i>used to be</i>
<i>the Blizzard Bunch's strength.</i>

16:41.130 --> 16:45.050
<i>But because of them,</i>
<i>our operations have been put on hold.</i>

16:51.220 --> 16:52.850
<i>I'll get my revenge.</i>

16:52.970 --> 16:55.310
<i>With the power of</i>
<i>the New Blizzard Bunch.</i>

16:59.400 --> 17:02.690
<i>I gave Dr. Kuseno a hard time</i>
<i>with my unreasonable request</i>

17:02.690 --> 17:06.740
<i>but following Master's advice,</i>
<i>I had him increase my power even more.</i>

17:07.200 --> 17:10.160
This upgrade is pretty reckless.

17:10.280 --> 17:13.450
A terribly unbalanced,
attack-specialized boost.

17:13.870 --> 17:18.500
I boosted the horsepower to the limit 
without reducing the armor.

17:18.750 --> 17:21.750
You'll have to fight while controlling
that power yourself.

17:22.170 --> 17:26.800
If you go full power, the parts will
exceed their endurance and break.

17:27.050 --> 17:31.640
It's strictly a last resort...
Ten seconds is the limit.

17:32.140 --> 17:34.560
Any more than that,
your body won’t withstand.

17:34.680 --> 17:36.930
If your energy core explodes

17:36.930 --> 17:40.230
even though you are a cyborg,
you could die.

17:40.810 --> 17:45.190
You got that, Genos?
Full power will only last 10 seconds.

17:45.570 --> 17:47.400
Don't forget that.

17:50.160 --> 17:50.990
Oh.

17:54.030 --> 17:55.660
What do you want now?

17:55.830 --> 17:58.710
Don't think you can visit
whenever you like.

17:59.080 --> 18:02.290
Oh, please. You're around
all the time too, aren't you?

18:02.420 --> 18:04.250
You don't get to complain.

18:04.630 --> 18:07.590
I have the right as Master's disciple.

18:08.170 --> 18:10.550
Besides, I'm paying my share
of the rent.

18:10.760 --> 18:14.970
Rent? Saitama isn't even
the owner of this apartment.

18:14.970 --> 18:16.640
He's just living here
without permission.

18:16.930 --> 18:18.560
You're getting scammed.

18:19.390 --> 18:23.150
Anyway, haven't you heard anything
from the Association yet?

18:23.270 --> 18:24.730
They've already contacted me.

18:25.440 --> 18:28.490
One of the executive's son has
been taken hostage,

18:28.650 --> 18:30.990
so I feel like they should have
made a move already.

18:31.240 --> 18:33.740
But maybe they haven't
located the hideout?

18:34.030 --> 18:37.540
If we knew, Master Saitama would've
wiped them all out by now.

18:38.200 --> 18:40.000
I'm back from getting repairs.

18:40.120 --> 18:41.620
We're here, Saitama.

18:41.670 --> 18:44.170
We can finally have a strategy meeting...

18:45.040 --> 18:46.840
Oh? He's not here.

18:47.170 --> 18:50.050
But the discount sale he was waiting for
is the day after tomorrow.

18:50.920 --> 18:52.180
Did he tell you anything?

18:52.220 --> 18:55.010
His hero suit is gone too.
Maybe something happened.

18:56.220 --> 18:59.850
Yo! We're back, Saitama.

19:00.100 --> 19:01.480
Master is not here.

19:01.640 --> 19:04.560
Hm? Not here? That's too bad.

19:05.360 --> 19:09.650
We were just about to raid
the monsters' hideout with King.

19:09.780 --> 19:12.740
What? So you've located
the Monster Association's hideout?

19:13.070 --> 19:15.570
Apparently, it's right nearby.

19:15.660 --> 19:17.370
Right under our noses,
as they say.

19:18.700 --> 19:20.620
You're coming too, won't you, Genos?

19:20.660 --> 19:21.660
Of course.

19:25.250 --> 19:28.000
Phew, I somehow
managed to get out.

19:28.880 --> 19:30.590
Oh, there you are King.

19:31.510 --> 19:33.930
Oh...Hi...

19:35.640 --> 19:37.180
Looks like everyone's here.

19:37.220 --> 19:39.180
Saitama's not here though.

19:39.260 --> 19:40.720
What? No way!

19:40.720 --> 19:43.560
But we don't have any time left
before the attack begins...

19:43.730 --> 19:49.940
RUMBLE RUMBLE

19:43.940 --> 19:45.520
So what do we do, King?

19:45.900 --> 19:47.900
Do we wait for Saitama
to come back?

19:48.020 --> 19:49.940
Or do we go in without him?

19:49.980 --> 19:52.900
RUMBLE RUMBLE

19:53.240 --> 19:54.700
We wait for Saitama.

19:55.360 --> 19:56.990
If this is going to be
an all-out battle

19:56.990 --> 19:59.080
we need Saitama's strength.

19:59.370 --> 20:00.740
I gotta hand it to you, King.

20:00.870 --> 20:03.210
You already made plans
behind the scenes.

20:03.540 --> 20:05.620
If we're going, then we all go.

20:05.830 --> 20:09.460
All of the members of
this New Blizzard Bunch together, right?

20:09.550 --> 20:10.710
So what should we do?

20:11.840 --> 20:14.840
Hey you! Don't ignore me!

20:14.930 --> 20:20.220
Hey, are you listening!
Look at me! Hey!

20:20.600 --> 20:24.770
King’s delay only increases
the burden on the other Class‑S heroes.

20:24.890 --> 20:26.270
You guys go on ahead.

20:26.600 --> 20:27.980
I will wait for Master.

20:28.520 --> 20:30.270
Once he returns, we'll join the raid.

20:30.360 --> 20:32.070
Sounds like a plan.

20:32.070 --> 20:34.400
<i>What? We're going without Saitama?</i>

20:34.440 --> 20:35.820
<i>Are you serious?</i>

20:36.780 --> 20:38.120
All right, let's go.

20:38.320 --> 20:40.370
Let's finish this before sundown.

20:40.490 --> 20:44.040
Follow me!
The New Blizzard Bunch, head out!

20:44.040 --> 20:47.880
RUMBLE RUMBLE

20:45.910 --> 20:47.330
<i>I'm not sure about this...</i>

20:51.000 --> 20:53.920
<i>Saitama, where did you go?</i>

22:31.600 --> 22:32.730
We've arrived.

22:36.940 --> 22:39.360
Hm? Where's King?

22:39.570 --> 22:41.240
He should've been at the rear.

22:41.280 --> 22:43.280
I saw him running off.

22:43.620 --> 22:47.490
<i>I'm gonna get to my position early,</i>
<i>so don't worry about me.</i>

22:47.620 --> 22:50.660
<i>Everyone should stick to</i>
<i>your scheduled timing for the assault.</i>

22:51.080 --> 22:52.170
That's what he said.

22:52.330 --> 22:56.210
He acts on his own like it's nothing.

22:56.500 --> 22:58.590
<i>Why didn't he tell me directly?</i>

22:59.630 --> 23:01.840
<i>Am I still being treated like a kid?</i>

23:01.970 --> 23:06.850
He acts fast. That's just how he is.

23:07.140 --> 23:10.480
I was hoping to see King
in action up close.

23:10.560 --> 23:11.640
What a shame.

23:11.770 --> 23:14.230
He has his own way
of doing things.

23:14.600 --> 23:15.480
Yeah.

23:15.610 --> 23:16.520
Hey...

23:17.110 --> 23:18.690
Check out what's ahead.

23:19.740 --> 23:22.150
Looks like they're rolling out
the welcome party for us.

23:22.360 --> 23:24.740
Whoa... They just keep showing up.

23:25.160 --> 23:28.200
Master Atomic,
I sense them behind us too.

23:28.620 --> 23:30.580
Not just behind us.

23:39.340 --> 23:41.260
<i>An old rag...?</i>

23:45.840 --> 23:47.680
Well, well...

23:48.010 --> 23:49.510
Oh my...

23:49.510 --> 23:53.310
I heard the Hero Association was
sending in its full fighting force

23:53.310 --> 23:55.060
but this is it?

23:55.850 --> 24:00.630
COUNTERSTRIKE
